From 6be028b653cf74a71f7273e47362690a6b792c9d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ivory <contact@ivory.cafe>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 23:17:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/9] Let Manifest namespaces define a bounded force-capture
 scope

Use manifest-derived namespace prefixes when an exact force selector is absent, preserve explicit selector behavior, and align persisted fallbacks with the accepted Manager defaults.

Constraint: Manifest-scoped capture must remain bounded by class, method, and attempt budgets.

Rejected: Require an exact class and method selector for every force capture | It prevents automatic coverage of manifest-owned namespaces.

Confidence: high

Scope-risk: moderate

Directive: Preserve deterministic namespace ordering and shared validation semantics across Framework, Manager, and ART.

Tested: source contract validation; m -j8 framework-minus-apex; userdebug framework replacement and post-flash validation.
Change-Id: Ifb1eb177c960b98795a34622caa8b740ca388db9
